{
  "mn3:0.1": "Middle Discourses 3 ",
  "mn3:0.2": "Heirs in the Teaching ",
  "mn3:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn3:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn3:1.3": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "mn3:1.4": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "mn3:1.5": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn3:1.6": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "mn3:2.1": "“Mendicants, be my heirs in the teaching, not in things of the flesh. ",
  "mn3:2.2": "Out of sympathy for you, I think, ",
  "mn3:2.3": "‘How can my disciples become heirs in the teaching, not in things of the flesh?’ ",
  "mn3:2.4": "If you become heirs in things of the flesh, not in the teaching, that will make you liable to the accusation: ",
  "mn3:2.5": "‘The Teacher’s disciples live as heirs in things of the flesh, not in the teaching.’ ",
  "mn3:2.6": "And it will make me liable to the accusation: ",
  "mn3:2.7": "‘The Teacher’s disciples live as heirs in things of the flesh, not in the teaching.’ ",
  "mn3:2.8": "If you become heirs in the teaching, not in things of the flesh, that will make you not liable to the accusation: ",
  "mn3:2.9": "‘The Teacher’s disciples live as heirs in the teaching, not in things of the flesh.’ ",
  "mn3:2.10": "And it will make me not liable to the accusation: ",
  "mn3:2.11": "‘The Teacher’s disciples live as heirs in the teaching, not in things of the flesh.’ ",
  "mn3:2.12": "So, mendicants, be my heirs in the tea